  "worked_solution": "We start by drawing a diagram of the situation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066033/assets/1109f4736ddfa81344d545802438588967aa18aac379c75a6b7be58688fb931f.png)\n\nIn the diagram:\n\n- $x$ is the distance between snowplow $F$ and the maintenance station $T$\n\n- $y$ is the distance between snowplow $E$ and the maintenance station $T$\n\n- $z$ is the distance between the snowplows.\n\nBoth snowplows are moving toward $T$, so the leg rates are negative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dx}{dt} & =-10\\text{\u00a0}\\text{mph} \\\\ \\frac{dy}{dt} & =-24\\text{\u00a0}\\text{mph}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, compute $z$ using the Pythagorean Theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ {6}^{2}+{8}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ 36+64 & ={z}^{2} \\\\ {z}^{2} & =100 \\\\ z & =10\\text{\u00a0}\\text{mi}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={z}^{2}$ with respect to $t$ and substitute the known values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x\\frac{dx}{dt}+2y\\frac{dy}{dt} & =2z\\frac{dz}{dt} \\\\ 2(6)(-10)+2(8)(-24) & =2(10)\\frac{dz}{dt} \\\\ -120-384 & =20\\frac{dz}{dt} \\\\ -504 & =20\\frac{dz}{dt} \\\\ \\frac{dz}{dt} & \u2248-25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nSo, the speed of convergence of the two snowplows is approximately $25\\text{\u00a0}\\text{mph}.$",
